---
description: Rules for handling forms with Server Actions in Next.js
globs: next-app/app/**/*.tsx
alwaysApply: false
---
[nextjs.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/nextjs.mdc)
[nextjs-server-actions.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/nextjs-server-actions.mdc)

- Forms must be in Client Components (mark with `'use client'`)
- Use `useActionState` hook from React for form state management
- Import Server Actions from `@/app/actions/*`
- Pass action to `useActionState(action, initialState)` as first parameter
- Use `formAction` from `useActionState` as the `action` prop on `<form>`
- Display errors from action state: `{state?.error && <div>{state.error}</div>}`
- Display success messages: `{state?.success && state?.message && <div>{state.message}</div>}`
- Use `isPending` from `useActionState` to disable form inputs during submission
- Use proper form inputs with `name` attributes matching Server Action expectations
- Use shadcn/ui form components (`Input`, `Label`, `Button`, etc.) for consistent styling
- Set appropriate `autoComplete` attributes for accessibility
- Handle loading states with disabled inputs and loading text on buttons
